<title>FINLAND: VIKING LINE SIX-MTH PASSENGER VOLUME DOWN.</title>
<headline>VIKING LINE SIX-MTH PASSENGER VOLUME DOWN.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish Baltic Sea ferry operator Viking Line said on Wednesday the volume of passengers it carried in the six-month period to end-April fell 6.1 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>&quot;During the period November 1, 1996 - April 30, 1997, Viking Line carried more than 1.9 million passengers,&quot; it said in a statement.  </p>
<p>Viking Line gave the following figures:</p>
<p>			  Nov/96-Apr/97  Nov/95/Apr/96</p>
<p> Route			    passengers	    change (pct)</p>
<p> Turku-Stockholm	  837,067	814,807	   +2.7</p>
<p> Helsinki-Stockholm     491,259	520,761	   -5.7</p>
<p> Helsinki-Tallinn	 621,046	741,452	  -16.2</p>
<p> TOTAL		    1,949,372    2,077,020	   -6.1</p>
<p> Cars			 121,266	128,344	   -5.5</p>
<p> Cargo units		 36,710	 36,812	   -0.3</p>
<p>--Helsinki Newsroom, +3589 680 50 235, news@reuters.fi</p>
